# Benchmark + test scratch.
#
# The canonical recorded run and its charts ARE committed: the README quotes
# numbers from them, and the project's rule is that every published number
# traces to a recorded file with the command that produced it. Ignoring them
# would leave that record only on the machine that happened to run it.
bench/results/*
!bench/results/results.json
!bench/results/writes_durable.png
!bench/results/writes_buffered.png
!bench/results/reads.png
!bench/results/write_amplification.png
*.sst
*.log
MANIFEST-*
CURRENT
LOCK

# Course materials and personal study notes.
#
# These are the inputs the engine was built from plus a private readiness
# checklist, not part of the engine itself. They stay on disk; the public
# reading guide is docs/STUDY.md.
documentation/

